FFTW genfft DCT codelets
------------------------

The files:

    src/cpu/bm/dct_codelet_fwd_n{12,16,32,64}_is{8,16}.hpp
    src/cpu/bm/dct_codelet_inv_n{12,16,32,64}_is{8,16}.hpp
    src/cuda/bm3d/dct_codelet_{fwd,inv}_n{12,16,32,64}_is8.hpp (copies of the files above)

are generated by FFTW genfft (`genfft/gen_r2r.ml`) and are distributed under
the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later.

Copyright (c) 1997-1999 Massachusetts Institute of Technology
Copyright (c) 2003, 2007-14 Matteo Frigo
Copyright (c) 2003, 2007-14 Massachusetts Institute of Technology

They are compiled as Highway kernels through `src/cpu/bm/dct_codelet_adapter.hpp`
and as scalar device code through `src/cuda/bm3d/dct_codelets.cuh`.
This project does not link against libfftw3 and does not use the FFTW planner.

Regenerate with:

    tools/gen_dct_codelets.sh /path/to/gen_r2r.native [output-directory]

FFTW: https://www.fftw.org/
Source: https://github.com/FFTW/fftw3

DA3D
----

src/cpu/da3d/da3d.cpp adapts the DA3D reference implementation
(https://github.com/gfacciol/da3d, IPOL 2017, https://doi.org/10.5201/ipol.2017.203):
the tile split, the weight map pyramid and the per-patch steps follow it.
tests/da3d_ref/ipol-tiles.patch is a patch against that implementation. The
